Attributions for Apache-2.0 material
------------------------------------

Some pin and clock constraints (gowin/p1/sdr.cst, gowin/p1/sdr.sdc, gowin/ladder/), the
SerDes parameter files (gowin/p1/ip/serdes/) and the DDR3 settings (hw/gowin/mem/gwmc_param.v)
follow the Tang Mega 138K Pro examples by Sipeed (Shenzhen Sipeed Technology Co., Ltd.), licensed
under the Apache License 2.0.


Not in this repository
----------------------

Slint (SixtyFPS GmbH, https://slint.dev) is fetched by Cargo when the firmware is built. It is used under the
GNU General Public License version 3 only.

The test recordings (WSJT-X sample recordings, Codec 2 speech files, FreeDV sample signals) are fetched by
tools/fetch_test_audio.sh and tools/fetch_freedv_test.sh from their own projects and are not part of this
repository. The FT8 test vectors are made from the WSJT-X recordings by tools/make_ft8_vectors.sh at test time.


Built firmware and bitstream
----------------------------

The firmware image built from fw/ is one combined work. It contains Slint (used under the GNU General Public
License version 3 only), mfsk-core and the FT8 files listed above (GPL-3.0 or later), and tr-codec2 and
tr-freedv (used under the GPL by section 3 of the LGPL 2.1). A firmware image is therefore distributed under
the GNU General Public License version 3, and its complete source is this repository at the same commit
together with the crates named in fw/Cargo.lock. The image also contains crates under the MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD,
Zlib and 0BSD licenses, whose notices must accompany it.

A bitstream built from rtl/ contains Gowin Semiconductor's encrypted IP (the AE350 RISC-V SoC with its Andes
core, the DDR3 memory controller and the SerDes PHY), which is not part of this repository and is generated from
a licensed Gowin EDA installation under Gowin's own terms. No bitstream and no firmware image is distributed
with this repository.
